-- title:
--   Group-like elements reduce to 1; dual has no nontrivial idempotents
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a Noetherian principal ideal domain with fraction field $F$, let $A$ be a commutative cocommutative Hopf $O$-algebra which is finite and free as an $O$-module, and let $L$ be a field which is an algebra over both $F$ and $O$ compatibly. Let $v$ be a valuation on $L$ with values in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero, satisfying $v(\mathrm{alg}_{O\to L}(r))\le 1$ for all $r\in O$; write $O_v$ for its valuation subring and $\mathfrak m_v$ for the maximal ideal of $O_v$. Let $S$ be a finite submonoid of the convolution monoid `WithConv` of $F$-algebra maps $F\otimes_O A\to L$, and let $\mathrm{ptSet}\,S$ be the set of such maps whose convolution class lies in $S$; let $I$ be the ideal of elements of $F\otimes_O A$ killed by all $\nu\in\mathrm{ptSet}\,S$ and $\mathrm{pointQuot}\,S=(F\otimes_O A)/I$. Four hypotheses are imposed: the pairs of points separate, in the sense that an element of $\mathrm{pointQuot}\,S\otimes_F\mathrm{pointQuot}\,S$ annihilated by every map $x\otimes y\mapsto \nu(x)\nu'(y)$ with $\nu,\nu'\in\mathrm{ptSet}\,S$ is zero; $\mathrm{ptSet}\,S$ is stable under precomposition with the antipode of $F\otimes_O A$, up to replacing $\nu$ by some $\nu'$ in the set with the same underlying linear map $\nu\circ\mathrm{antipode}$; the evaluation map $\mathrm{evalQuot}\,S\colon L\otimes_F\mathrm{pointQuot}\,S\to (S\to L)$ is bijective; and every point reduces to the identity, i.e. $v\bigl(\nu(1\otimes a)-\varepsilon(a)\bigr)<1$ for all $\nu\in\mathrm{ptSet}\,S$ and $a\in A$, where $\varepsilon$ is the counit of $A$ and its value is mapped into $L$. Let $B=\mathrm{characterGenericFibre}$ be the $F$-subalgebra of $F\otimes_O\mathrm{CartierDual}\,O\,A$ generated by the functionals annihilating $I$ under base change of duals, and let $E_S=\mathrm{characterClosure}=\{g\in\mathrm{CartierDual}\,O\,A: 1\otimes g\in B\}$, an $O$-subalgebra; assume $B$ is comultiplication-stable and antipode-stable in the sense of [`IsComulStable`](def/FiniteFlat_ClosureHopf.html#L232) and [`IsAntipodeStable`](def/FiniteFlat_ClosureHopf.html#L284), so that $E_S$ carries the Hopf $O$-algebra structure [`closureHopfAlgebra`](def/FiniteFlat_ClosureHopfAlgebra.html#L299). The conclusion has two parts: first, every group-like element $d$ of $L\otimes_O E_S$ lies in the $O_v$-span of $\{1\otimes e : e\in E_S\}$ and satisfies $d-1\in\mathfrak m_v\cdot$ that span; second, every $f$ in the Cartier dual $\mathrm{CartierDual}\,O\,E_S$ (the $O$-dual of $E_S$ with its convolution product) with $f\cdot f=f$ equals $0$ or $1$.
--
--   This is the integral statement, on the Cartier-dual side, that the group-like elements of the character closure of a finite point monoid reducing to the identity are congruent to $1$ modulo the maximal ideal of the valuation ring, together with the resulting absence of nontrivial idempotents in the dual; the second assertion plays the role that connectedness of a finite flat group scheme plays classically. It feeds the analysis of multiplicative-type pieces of reduction kernels at the prime $2$, being cited by [`HopfAlgebra.characterClosure_point_eq_trivial_of_restrict_of_congr_two`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.characterClosure_point_eq_trivial_of_restrict_of_congr_two).
